				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">I'm sure most of you already know about this, but for as long as I have been on the net I never really gave much thought to passwords or security.  Bear in mind, I am a very active online gambler and have a decent amount of money at various poker sites as well as Neteller.  Recently I decided to change that fact and make my passwords more secure - but my problem was that my memory sucks ass.
<br />

<br />
So I went searching for some type of tool to help me out and I found <a href="http://passwordsafe.sourceforge.net/" target="_blank" class="postlink">http://passwordsafe.sourceforge.net/</a> (Password Safe) and I am simply in love with it.
<br />

<br />
Essentially it's a secure database of all of your passwords that you can organize by certain groups (ie. for me I have Banking, Work, Poker, Poker Affiliates, Email, etc.).  The database is password protected and that's the only password you need to remember.  After you get all your passwords into the database you simply double click the one that you want and it copies the password to your clipboard so you simply have to do a Cntrl-V to paste it in.   This will also keep you safe in case someone has a key logger installed on your computer.
<br />

<br />
Anyways, I don't want to plug this much and I figure most of you know about tools like this (or better ones), but for me it was a great find.  It will also generate secure passwords for you that you can use so for the first time ever each of my important passwords are different (and can no longer be cracked by opening a dictionary).[/url]<br />_________________<br />Sanadan Moonbow
